## Retrieve a model response

**get** `/api/v1/responses/{response_id}`

Retrieves a tenant-scoped stored Responses API response.

### Path Parameters

- `response_id: string`

### Header Parameters

- `"X-Organization-Id": optional string`

### Returns

- `Response object { id, object, created_at, 10 more }`

  - `id: string`

  - `object: "response"`

    - `"response"`

  - `created_at: optional number`

    Unix timestamp (in seconds) when the response was created.

  - `status: "completed" or "failed" or "in_progress" or 3 more`

    - `"completed"`

    - `"failed"`

    - `"in_progress"`

    - `"cancelled"`

    - `"queued"`

    - `"incomplete"`

  - `model: string`

    Public name of the model that generated the response.

  - `output: array of ResponseOutputItem`

    Items the model generated, in order.

    - `type: string`

      Item type, such as `message`, `reasoning`, `function_call`, `mcp_call`, `file_search_call` or `web_search_call`. Fields beyond the ones listed depend on the type.

    - `id: optional string`

      Identifier of the output item.

    - `status: optional string`

      Status of the item, such as `completed` or `in_progress`.

    - `role: optional "assistant"`

      Author of a `message` item.

[Source: https://docs.adaptionlabs.ai/api/resources/responses/ | Type: docs | Title: Responses | Published: unknown | Retrieved: 2026-11-17]
- `output_tokens_details: optional map[unknown]`

  - `previous_response_id: optional string`

    The response this one continues, if any.

  - `store: optional boolean`

    Whether the response is stored for later retrieval.

  - `metadata: optional map[string]`

### Example

```http
curl https://api.prod.adaptionlabs.ai/api/v1/responses/$RESPONSE_ID \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer $ADAPTION_API_KEY"
```

