# OpenCode

> Configure Adaption as an inference provider in OpenCode and code with Adaption models.

OpenCode can use Adaption’s hosted models as an inference provider. Adaption serves the OpenAI Responses API, so OpenCode’s compatible Responses runtime connects without a plugin. You bring an [Adaption API key](/introduction/create-api-keys/index.md) and a model ID from [Models](/inference-stacks/models/index.md).

You can also connect the [Adaption MCP server](/tools/mcp/index.md) separately to give OpenCode tools for interacting with the Adaption Platform.

## Create and export an API key

1. [Sign in](https://adaptionlabs.ai/app/auth) to Adaption.

2. Open [**Settings**](https://adaptionlabs.ai/app/settings), then [**API keys**](https://adaptionlabs.ai/app/settings?tab=api_keys).

3. Create a key and copy it. You will not be able to view the key again.

4. Export it as `ADAPTION_API_KEY` so OpenCode can read it automatically:

   Terminal window

   ```
   export ADAPTION_API_KEY="pt_live_..."
   ```

## Add the provider

OpenCode reads project configuration from `opencode.json(c)` or `.opencode/opencode.json(c)` in the current directory, and global configuration from `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json(c)`. Use the global file to make Adaption available in every project.

Adaption’s inference endpoint implements the Responses API, so the provider uses the compatible Responses runtime package:

opencode.jsonc

```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "providers": {
    "adaption": {
      "name": "Adaption",
      "env": ["ADAPTION_API_KEY"],
      "package": "@opencode/ai/providers/openai-compatible/responses",
      "settings": {
        "baseURL": "https://api.prod.adaptionlabs.ai/api/v1",
      },
      "models": {
        "qwen3.5-397b": {
          "name": "Qwen 3.5 397B",
        },
        "glm-5.2": {
          "name": "GLM 5.2",
        },
        "glm-5.3-flash": {
          "name": "GLM 5.3 Flash",
        },
        "deepseek-v4-flash": {
          "name": "DeepSeek V4 Flash",
        },
        "gemma-4-31b-it": {
          "name": "Gemma 4 31B IT",
        },
        "gemma-4-26b-a4b-it": {
          "name": "Gemma 4 26B A4B IT",
        },
        "qwen3.8-27b": {
          "name": "Qwen 3.8 27B",
        },
      },
    },
  },
}
```

`env` tells OpenCode to send `ADAPTION_API_KEY` as `Authorization: Bearer ...` on every request. API keys are bound to an organization, so no `X-Organization-Id` header is needed. Add or remove entries in `models` to match what your key can access; see [Models](/inference-stacks/models/index.md) for the full list.

Config changes apply without a restart. OpenCode watches the file and reloads providers after a save.

## Select a model

In the TUI, run `/models` and choose an entry. To set a default instead, set the top-level `model` field:

opencode.jsonc

[Source: https://docs.adaptionlabs.ai/tools/opencode/ | Type: docs | Title: OpenCode | Published: unknown | Retrieved: 2026-11-17]
```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "model": "adaption/qwen3.5-397b",
  "providers": {
    "adaption": {
      "env": ["ADAPTION_API_KEY"],
      "package": "@opencode/ai/providers/openai-compatible/responses",
      "settings": {
        "baseURL": "https://api.prod.adaptionlabs.ai/api/v1",
      },
      "models": {
        "qwen3.5-397b": { "name": "Qwen 3.5 397B" },
      },
    },
  },
}
```

Then ask OpenCode:

> Explain this repository to me.

The response comes from the Adaption Responses API. Streaming works the same way it does for any OpenCode model.

## Use an inference stack

An inference stack is a saved configuration of a model, tools, datasets, and memory. Pass its name as `stack:<name>` through the same provider.

Stacks belong to your account and cannot be auto-discovered, so add one as a model entry whose key follows the `stack:<name>` pattern. The key is also what Adaption receives as the `model`:

opencode.jsonc

```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "providers": {
    "adaption": {
      "env": ["ADAPTION_API_KEY"],
      "package": "@opencode/ai/providers/openai-compatible/responses",
      "settings": {
        "baseURL": "https://api.prod.adaptionlabs.ai/api/v1",
      },
      "models": {
        "stack:support-assistant": {
          "name": "Support Assistant Stack",
        },
      },
    },
  },
}
```

Select `adaption/stack:support-assistant` in `/models`, or set `"model": "adaption/stack:support-assistant"`. See [Key concepts](/inference-stacks/key-concepts/index.md) for how a stack’s model, tools, datasets, and memory apply to each request.

Stacks are only served by the Responses API. A provider configured with a chat-completions runtime instead of the `openai-compatible/responses` package can call hosted models, but stack calls fail with `model_not_found`.

## Optional: connect the MCP server

To let OpenCode call Adaption’s dataset and AutoScientist tools, add the hosted MCP server as well. The CLI preserves unrelated configuration:

Terminal window

```
opencode mcp add adaption --global --url https://api.prod.adaptionlabs.ai/api/v1/mcp
```

Then run `/mcps`, select the `adaption` server, and sign in with your Adaption account in the browser. No API key is needed for the MCP connection.

See [MCP](/tools/mcp/index.md) for the complete tool catalog. The MCP server is separate from the inference provider and does not affect model selection.

